WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.570
- [Narrator] Brazil takes
breast milk very seriously.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.880
It has over 200 milk banks nationwide,

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.890
the highest of any country.

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:11.600
But here's the weird part,
while the US has over

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.540
one and a half times the
population of Brazil,

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.680
it only has 24 milk banks,
which distribute less

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.480
than six million ounces
of breast milk a year.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.390
And that's a serious problem,
since intensive care units

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.710
alone demand over 63
million ounces annually,

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.640
so parents of healthy babies
need to find another way

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.045
to feed their kids and will turn to other,

00:00:32.045 --> 00:00:34.203
more obscure sources.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:39.490
Of course, many parents
have a built-in supply

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:41.136
of breast milk, free of charge.

00:00:41.136 --> 00:00:43.790
But not everyone can breastfeed.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.466
This might be because
they don't produce enough

00:00:45.466 --> 00:00:48.410
on their own, their work
schedule leaves little time

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:51.270
for breastfeeding, or they
simply don't have breasts

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.810
in the first place.

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:56.910
In fact, only an estimated
26% of North Americans

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.890
exclusively breastfed.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.640
So if you're short on
breast milk, many parents

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.560
will head to groups like
Human Milk 4 Human Babies,

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.709
which connects milk
donors with milk seekers.

00:01:06.709 --> 00:01:10.886
In this case, helping over
20,000 community members

00:01:10.886 --> 00:01:13.790
in 52 countries.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:16.440
But there's still not
enough milk to go around.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.820
That's where online marketplaces come in.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.700
On ad classified sites,
like Only The Breast,

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.940
and Breastfeeding Moms
Unite, people sell their milk

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.860
for around two dollars an ounce.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:29.420
That's a bargain compared
to over four dollars

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.140
that milk banks will charge.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.880
But this is a case of
you get what you pay for,

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:37.475
because the milk you might
receive may not be 100% human.

00:01:37.475 --> 00:01:38.370
(cow mooing)

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:41.760
In a 2015 study for example,
researchers ordered milk

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.723
from an anonymous online market.

00:01:43.723 --> 00:01:46.870
They tested the contents of
each sample and discovered

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.810
that one in every 10
samples was contaminated

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:52.840
with cow's milk, and by
a significant amount too.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.769
The contaminated samples
contained about 10% cow's milk.

00:01:55.769 --> 00:01:58.900
That's a lot more than a few drops.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:03.420
Moreover, a 2013 report
found that 74% of milk

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.620
from online markets
contained harmful bacteria,

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.550
which probably came from
poor collection, storage,

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:10.610
or shipping.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:13.560
All this begs the question,
why go through the hassle

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.480
and risk, when you can
easily grab some baby formula

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.300
at your local grocery?

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.090
Well, formula just doesn't cut it.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.960
Human breast milk is jam-packed
with brain developing

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:27.120
nutrients, disease-fighting
antibodies that jump-start

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.080
the immune system, and
helpful bacteria that rev up

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.846
the babies own gut flora.

00:02:31.846 --> 00:02:36.150
But baby formula has no
antibodies or bacteria

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.560
and that can make a huge difference.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.010
Researches calculated that over 800,000 

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.160
formula-fed infants who
die each year worldwide,

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.170
could have been saved by breastfeeding.

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:50.742
So parents are caught between
a rock and a hard place.

00:02:50.742 --> 00:02:54.540
Formula or mystery milk?

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:58.480
Fun fact, in Brazil, the
government funds couriers

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.780
on motorbikes to collect
breast milk directly

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.419
from people's houses.

00:03:02.419 --> 00:03:04.495
(clicking)

